# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overview {#overview}"
msgstr "Pangkalahatang-ideya {#overview}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Parity Twine Optimizer allows users to solve optimization problems with quantum computers using the [Parity Twine method](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.14020).\n"
"This approach, built on the Parity Architecture, uses the ParityQC compiler to minimize the gate counts and circuit depth required to run a quantum algorithm while accounting for device connectivity.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipinapahintulot ng Parity Twine Optimizer sa mga user na lutasin ang mga optimization problem gamit ang quantum computers sa pamamagitan ng [Parity Twine method](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.14020).\n"
"Ang approach na ito, na binuo sa ibabaw ng Parity Architecture, ay gumagamit ng ParityQC compiler para bawasan ang gate counts at circuit depth na kinakailangan para magpatakbo ng quantum algorithm habang isinasaalang-alang ang device connectivity.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This resource reduction enables solving industry-relevant optimization problems for sizes that are unfeasible with standard, SWAP-heavy, transpilation methods.\n"
"The Parity Twine Optimizer automates transpilation steps and can be used with minimal user input.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pagbawas na ito sa resource ay nagbibigay-daan sa paglutas ng mga optimization problem na mahalaga sa industriya para sa mga sukat na hindi kayang lutasin ng standard, SWAP-heavy, transpilation methods.\n"
"Inaawtomatiko ng Parity Twine Optimizer ang mga transpilation step at maaaring gamitin nang minimal ang input ng user.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Parity Twine approach outperforms all other compilation methods in terms of reducing gate counts and circuit depths for quantum algorithms such as the\n"
"[quantum approximate optimization algorithm (QAOA)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.14020) and [quantum Fourier transform (QFT)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.12465).\n"
"By abstracting quantum information away from the physical qubits, non-local interactions are implemented without SWAP gates. Instead, Parity Twine chains (sequences of CNOT gates) systematically distribute logical\n"
"parity information between qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nauunahan ng Parity Twine approach ang lahat ng ibang compilation method sa pagbawas ng gate counts at circuit depths para sa mga quantum algorithm tulad ng\n"
"[quantum approximate optimization algorithm (QAOA)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.14020) at [quantum Fourier transform (QFT)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.12465).\n"
"Sa pamamagitan ng pag-abstract ng quantum information palayo sa physical qubits, naipapatupad ang non-local interactions nang walang SWAP gates. Sa halip, ang Parity Twine chains (mga sequence ng CNOT gates) ay sistematikong ipinamamahagi ang logical\n"
"parity information sa pagitan ng mga qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The optimizer uses the QAOA to minimize the energy of a given cost function. QAOA is a hybrid quantum-classical variational algorithm designed to solve combinatorial optimization problems by approximating the ground state\n"
"of a cost Hamiltonian ($H_C$). A mixing term ($H_B$) drives transitions between states to explore the solution space. An alternating sequence of these terms, controlled by parameters $\\gamma$ and $\\beta$, defines the unitary\n"
"$U(\\gamma, \\beta) = \\Pi_{i=1}^p e^{-i \\beta_i H_B} e^{-i \\gamma_i H_C}$, which acts on the initial state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ginagamit ng optimizer ang QAOA para bawasan ang energy ng ibinigay na cost function. Ang QAOA ay isang hybrid quantum-classical variational algorithm na dinisenyo para lutasin ang combinatorial optimization problem sa pamamagitan ng pagtantiya sa ground state\n"
"ng cost Hamiltonian ($H_C$). Ang mixing term ($H_B$) ay nagtutulak ng mga transition sa pagitan ng mga estado para tuklasin ang solution space. Ang alternating sequence ng mga terminong ito, na kinokontrol ng mga parameter na $\\gamma$ at $\\beta$, ay tumutukoy sa unitary\n"
"$U(\\gamma, \\beta) = \\Pi_{i=1}^p e^{-i \\beta_i H_B} e^{-i \\gamma_i H_C}$, na kumikilos sa paunang estado.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Encoding of the problem unitary, exp($-i \\beta H_C)$), requires encoding of all logical $n$-body rotation operators (exp($-i \\beta J_{i,j,...n}Z_iZ_j...Z_n$)).\n"
"This can be accomplished using $n$-body generators (Parity Twine Networks), which reduce the QAOA circuit depth and two-qubit gate count.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pag-encode ng problem unitary, exp($-i \\beta H_C)$), ay nangangailangan ng pag-encode ng lahat ng logical $n$-body rotation operators (exp($-i \\beta J_{i,j,...n}Z_iZ_j...Z_n$)).\n"
"Maaari itong maisagawa gamit ang $n$-body generators (Parity Twine Networks), na binabawasan ang QAOA circuit depth at two-qubit gate count.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Description {#description}"
msgstr "Deskripsyon {#description}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Parity Twine Optimizer input consists of an optimization problem, the chosen IBM Quantum hardware name, and additional optional arguments to tailor the transpilation and hardware execution settings. The optimizer\n"
"function routes the problem definition to the Parity Twine Compiler. Figure 1 shows a summary of the function workflow.\n"
msgstr ""
"Binubuo ang input ng Parity Twine Optimizer ng optimization problem, ang napiling pangalan ng IBM Quantum hardware, at karagdagang optional arguments para i-tailor ang mga setting ng transpilation at hardware execution. Ina-route ng optimizer\n"
"function ang problem definition papunta sa Parity Twine Compiler. Ipinapakita ng Figure 1 ang buod ng function workflow.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Parity Twine Optimizer workflow](/docs/images/guides/parity-twine-optimizer/process_pipeline.avif \"Figure 1: Summary of the Parity Twine Optimizer workflow.\")\n"
msgstr "![Parity Twine Optimizer workflow](/docs/images/guides/parity-twine-optimizer/process_pipeline.avif \"Figure 1: Summary of the Parity Twine Optimizer workflow.\")\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The input optimization problem is pre-processed into a (normalized) Hamiltonian. The ParityQC compiler then constructs a parameterized Parity Twine ansatz circuit, which is transpiled to a logical ansatz matching the native\n"
"gate set of the chosen hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang input optimization problem ay pre-processed papunta sa isang (normalized) Hamiltonian. Pagkatapos ay bumubuo ang ParityQC compiler ng parameterized Parity Twine ansatz circuit, na tine-transpile papunta sa logical ansatz na tumutugma sa native\n"
"gate set ng napiling hardware.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"QAOA circuit parameters are classically optimized using the [\"efficient depth one\"](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qaoa_training_pipeline/blob/main/how_tos/efficient_depth_one.ipynb) approach and assigned to the transpiled circuit.\n"
"As one round of QAOA is used, optimal $\\gamma$ and $\\beta$ parameters are obtained using a grid search on a CPU without the need for costly iterative optimization\n"
"over many circuit calls. This greatly minimizes the required QPU runtime of the optimizer. Execution time per circuit is mostly determined by the constant overhead to run a job on the QPU.\n"
"With the circuit parameters set, the job is submitted to the specified IBM&reg; QPU.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang QAOA circuit parameters ay classically optimized gamit ang [\"efficient depth one\"](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qaoa_training_pipeline/blob/main/how_tos/efficient_depth_one.ipynb) approach at inilalapat sa transpiled circuit.\n"
"Dahil isang round lang ng QAOA ang ginagamit, ang optimal na $\\gamma$ at $\\beta$ parameters ay nakukuha gamit ang grid search sa CPU nang hindi na kailangan ng magastos na iterative optimization\n"
"sa maraming circuit call. Malaki ang naitutulong nito sa pagbawas ng kinakailangang QPU runtime ng optimizer. Ang execution time kada circuit ay pangunahing tinutukoy ng constant overhead sa pagpapatakbo ng job sa QPU.\n"
"Matapos itakda ang circuit parameters, isinusumite ang job sa itinalagang IBM&reg; QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Raw results are then post-processed. This step uses a local greedy search that iterates randomly through the solution string and flips bit values if this reduces the value of the cost function.\n"
msgstr "Ang raw results ay pagkatapos post-processed. Ginagamit ng hakbang na ito ang local greedy search na umuulit nang random sa solution string at binabaligtad ang bit values kung ito ay nagpapababa sa value ng cost function.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Benchmarks {#benchmarks}"
msgstr "Mga Benchmark {#benchmarks}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Disclaimer\">\n"
"Performance can depend on both the problem instance and subsequent processing steps. In some cases, classical samples and quantum-generated samples might achieve similar final solution quality after equivalent post-processing. Evaluation should therefore consider the complete optimization workflow.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Paalala\">\n"
"Maaaring depende ang performance sa parehong problem instance at sa mga susunod na processing step. Sa ilang kaso, ang classical samples at quantum-generated samples ay maaaring magkaroon ng magkatulad na final solution quality matapos ang equivalent post-processing. Kaya dapat isaalang-alang ng evaluation ang kabuuang optimization workflow.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

