msgid "Use `catalog.backends()` to see a list of available backends from the user account/instance.\n"
msgstr "Gamitin ang `catalog.backends()` para makita ang listahan ng mga available na backend mula sa user account/instance.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If no backend is specified, the least-busy backend (the one with the least number of pending jobs) is automatically selected.\n"
msgstr "Kung walang tinukoy na backend, ang least-busy backend (ang isa na may pinakakaunting pending jobs) ang awtomatikong napipili.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Once the optimizer is loaded (see previous), you can run it on the problem using default options:\n"
msgstr "Kapag na-load na ang optimizer (tingnan sa nakaraan), maaari mo itong patakbuhin sa problema gamit ang default options:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check the job status as follows:\n"
msgstr "Suriin ang job status gaya ng sumusunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Retrieve results as follows:\n"
msgstr "Kunin ang mga resulta gaya ng sumusunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Printing the results gives the following:\n"
msgstr "Ang pag-print ng mga resulta ay nagbibigay ng sumusunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `solution` dictionary corresponds to the qubits defined in the problem ($s_0, s_1$, and $s_2$) and gives their optimized spin values.\n"
msgstr "Ang `solution` dictionary ay tumutugma sa mga qubit na tinukoy sa problema ($s_0, s_1$, at $s_2$) at ibinibigay ang kanilang optimized spin values.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `objective_value` is the cost or energy of the optimization problem. It quantifies the `solution` quality.\n"
msgstr "Ang `objective_value` ay ang cost o energy ng optimization problem. Sinusukat nito ang kalidad ng `solution`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`metadata` gives information on the transpilation (two-qubit gate counts/depth, gates used, active qubits) and various runtimes for both quantum and classical compute time.\n"
msgstr "Ang `metadata` ay nagbibigay ng impormasyon tungkol sa transpilation (two-qubit gate counts/depth, mga ginamit na gate, active qubits) at iba't ibang runtime para sa parehong quantum at classical compute time.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Additionally, `metadata` provides a glimpse into the internal workings of the algorithm. You can see the optimized variational parameters (beta and gamma) and review how the distribution of measured bitstrings improved after classical post-processing was applied to the raw quantum results.\n"
msgstr "Bukod pa rito, ibinibigay ng `metadata` ang isang tingin sa internal workings ng algorithm. Makikita mo ang optimized variational parameters (beta at gamma) at masusuri kung paano bumuti ang distribution ng measured bitstrings matapos ilapat ang classical post-processing sa raw quantum results.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"All bitstrings in the result output can be mapped to the problem variables by using the `variable_mapping`.\n"
"For example, you can map the `'solution_bitstring': '100'` with the `'variable_mapping': {'0': 0, '1': 1, '2': 2}` to the binary solution: `{'0': 1, '1': 0, '2': 0}`.\n"
"Since you are solving the problem in terms of spin variables, you need to apply the binary to spin transformation  (`0` -> `1`, `1` -> `-1` ).\n"
"You then arrive at the final solution `'solution': {'0': -1, '1': 1, '2': 1}`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lahat ng bitstrings sa result output ay maaaring i-map sa mga problem variable gamit ang `variable_mapping`.\n"
"Halimbawa, maaari mong i-map ang `'solution_bitstring': '100'` gamit ang `'variable_mapping': {'0': 0, '1': 1, '2': 2}` papunta sa binary solution: `{'0': 1, '1': 0, '2': 0}`.\n"
"Dahil nilulutas mo ang problema sa termino ng spin variables, kailangan mong ilapat ang binary to spin transformation  (`0` -> `1`, `1` -> `-1` ).\n"
"Sa huli, dadating ka sa final solution `'solution': {'0': -1, '1': 1, '2': 1}`.\n"

